{"id": "EUVD-2026-55264", "enisaUuid": "c70fe3cb-73e8-34ac-9fd1-54ef26f20c84", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix path resolution in ksmbd_vfs_kern_path_create\n\nThe SMB2 open lookup is rooted at the share with LOOKUP_BENEATH, but the\ncreate/mkdir/hardlink sink is not: ksmbd_vfs_kern_path_create() builds an\nabsolute path with convert_to_unix_name() and resolves it from AT_FDCWD\nvia start_creating_path(), so a \"..\" component is walked from the real\nfilesystem root and escapes the export.\n\nAn authenticated client races a missing path component so the rooted open\nlookup returns -ENOENT (taking the create branch) while the same component\nis present (a directory) when the create walk runs; the create then\nresolves \"..\" out of the share.\n\nRoot the create walk at the share like the lookup and rename paths already\nare: resolve the parent with vfs_path_parent_lookup(..., LOOKUP_BENEATH,\n&share_conf->vfs_path) and create the final component with\nstart_creating_noperm(). convert_to_unix_name() then has no callers and is\nremoved.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T11:41:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:28", "baseScore": 9.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a2516be69048856e2a49a51e00975dc59431f95c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/489d1ded01425c0fb33418172c0e4e588467526b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c7c884a1305aa4540eb7942a50bd356b34120e1f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/98185b3025beeae92d1fe700d5db26b9ac4bf025", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c8951963d8ed357f70f59e0ad4ddce2199d2016"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fxqh-hm36-rrq9", "CVE-2026-68083"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.44, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "038b20ec-7250-3eac-83c6-c6dd0150612f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "06e6f01f-45fd-34be-9ee3-44b33c87a6d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "0d2599cc-28ac-3877-9edc-fa9fd257ec61", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "265fd1991c1db85fbabaad4946ca0e63e2ae688d <489d1ded01425c0fb33418172c0e4e588467526b"}, {"id": "406b0ae0-a2cb-3d14-86ef-f6ee828be085", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "503ececa-f5ce-31c2-b7f9-560fb6b02b8a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "77b56fdb-8f93-370f-9870-7196ff9ab2b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "265fd1991c1db85fbabaad4946ca0e63e2ae688d <1c8951963d8ed357f70f59e0ad4ddce2199d2016"}, {"id": "7d893573-7ab0-3fd9-a706-e9e5b6cfd77b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "265fd1991c1db85fbabaad4946ca0e63e2ae688d <c7c884a1305aa4540eb7942a50bd356b34120e1f"}, {"id": "b94d2ecd-568a-35e7-8c45-df42bf2a2c8e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "265fd1991c1db85fbabaad4946ca0e63e2ae688d <98185b3025beeae92d1fe700d5db26b9ac4bf025"}, {"id": "cb9b889f-a75b-3e77-9651-446eccef6db7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "e2ffd387-e808-3c34-8257-75dc2b1b8a13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "ea515687-99f1-35d2-a918-3ca97af9c505", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "f592d85c-a1ae-3231-bc36-9596a0e53c39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "265fd1991c1db85fbabaad4946ca0e63e2ae688d <a2516be69048856e2a49a51e00975dc59431f95c"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "02b452bb-c0d1-3910-bd19-2e5fba668c16", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}